# 🚀 Git & GitHub Useful Commands Cheat Sheet

> A quick reference for beginners to understand and interact with Git and GitHub.
> Prepared for practical project workflows.

---

# 🔧 1. Initial Git Setup

### Configure username

```bash
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
```

### Configure email

```bash
git config --global user.email "your@email.com"
```

### View global config

```bash
git config --global --list
```

---

# 📁 2. Local Repository Commands

### Initialize a repository

```bash
git init
```

### Check repository status

```bash
git status
```

### View changes in files

```bash
git diff
```

### View commit history

```bash
git log --oneline
```

---

# 📦 3. Staging & Commit Commands

### Add all files to staging

```bash
git add .
```

### Add specific file

```bash
git add filename
```

### Commit changes

```bash
git commit -m "Your message"
```

### Commit tracked files quickly

```bash
git commit -am "Your message"
```

---

# 🌐 4. Remote Repository Commands

### Add remote repository

```bash
git remote add origin <repo-url>
```

### View remote repositories

```bash
git remote -v
```

### Remove remote

```bash
git remote remove origin
```

### Change remote URL

```bash
git remote set-url origin <new-url>
```

---

# 🚀 5. Push & Pull Commands

### First push (set upstream)

```bash
git push -u origin main
```

### Push changes (after first time)

```bash
git push
```

### Pull latest changes

```bash
git pull origin main
```

### Clone repository

```bash
git clone <repo-url>
```

---

# 🌿 6. Branching Commands

### List branches

```bash
git branch
```

### Create new branch

```bash
git branch branch-name
```

### Switch branch

```bash
git switch branch-name
```

### Create and switch branch

```bash
git checkout -b branch-name
```

### Merge branch

```bash
git merge branch-name
```

---

# 🗑️ 7. Removing Files

### Remove file completely

```bash
git rm filename
```

### Remove folder

```bash
git rm -r foldername
```

### Stop tracking but keep locally

```bash
git rm --cached filename
```

---

# 🔍 8. Useful Inspection Commands

### Show current branch

```bash
git branch --show-current
```

### Show remote details

```bash
git remote show origin
```

### Show configuration source

```bash
git config --list --show-origin
```

---

# ⚡ 9. Daily Workflow (Recommended)

```bash
git add .
git commit -m "update"
git push
```

---

# 🎯 10. First Time Project Upload Workflow

```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git remote add origin <repo-url>
git push -u origin main
```

---

# 🧠 Pro Tips

* Write meaningful commit messages
* Use branches for new features
* Push code regularly
* Always use .gitignore for sensitive files
* Keep your GitHub profile active

